.TH CCOL_R_MEMPOOL_TOTAL_CAPACITY 3 "2026-09-17" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_r_mempool_total_capacity \- get total capacity for a size
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cmempool.h>

size_t ccol_r_mempool_total_capacity(ccol_r_mempool *rmp, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the total number of entries in the pool that services the given
size. Does not include dynamic allocations.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
rmp   Ranged memory pool to query
size  Size in bytes to query (maps to a specific sub-pool)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns total capacity for this size
Returns 0 on error
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Returns 0 if size is invalid (0 or > largest_size)
Size is rounded up to next power-of-2 pool
Thread-safe if pool created with single_threaded=false

The count this reports for a size is the count that tier was built for,
and that many entries of that size are always obtainable. A tier large
enough to maintain per-thread caches allocates a reserve beyond it, so
concurrent callers can briefly hold a few more than this at once; see
ccol_mempool_total_capacity(3) for the full account.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_r_mempool_used_count (3),
.BR ccol_r_mempool_dynamic_allocs_count (3)
